{
  "configuration_id": "config_016",
  "reason": "Evidence: We have only one data point (config_001: rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000 → 48.5% acc), which is a modest baseline. The most critical uncertainty is whether adding the image modality provides any benefit over RNA alone, since this determines whether the entire multimodal search direction is worthwhile. Question: config_016 (multimodal, pca_n2000, resnet50, singleprofile, concat) is the minimal extension of config_001—only the image encoder and fusion are added—so it cleanly isolates the contribution of image information to the existing RNA baseline. Why this is the best next step: With 8 experiments remaining, we must first determine if multimodal is a promising direction before investing budget in exploring aggregation, fusion, encoder, or profile variations within it. A direct head-to-head comparison (same RNA encoder, same profile setting, only image added) gives the highest information gain per experiment and prevents wasting budget on complex multimodal variants if the image signal is weak or unhelpful."
}

